<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Abstract base for AAH archotech android body-part items. Mirrors VREA's own
    VREA_BodyPartAndroidBase idiom one level down, hoisting the fields every
    archotech AAH part shares:

      - techLevel Archotech (vs VREA base's Ultra default)
      - the AAH_BodyPartsAndroidArchotech thing category
      - the archotech part icon (Items/AAH_AndroidPart_Archotech)
      - recipeMaker Inherit="False"

    recipeMaker Inherit="False" suppresses VREA_BodyPartAndroidBase's recipeMaker
    so no Make recipe is auto-generated at the android workbench. Every AAH part
    instead defines an explicit crafting RecipeDef with allowMixingIngredients,
    required to resolve MinifiedThing ingredients (power cells, emanators, persona
    cores) — the auto-generated recipe's NoMix ingredient search can't unwrap
    minified buildings. See any RecipeDefs_*.xml for the full rationale.

    Each child keeps a costList only to satisfy the def validator (an
    Inherit="False" recipeMaker still requires a costList or costStuffCount); it
    is not used for crafting. Where a child also sets an explicit MarketValue, the
    costList does not drive price either (see that child's comment).

    NOT used by AAH_GravReactor: it's ultratech, so it keeps VREA's Ultra tech
    level and default blue icon and parents VREA_BodyPartAndroidBase directly.
    AAH_ThanaticReactor uses this base but re-overrides graphicData to the dark
    archotech variant.
  -->
  <ThingDef Name="AAH_BodyPartAndroidArchotechBase" ParentName="VREA_BodyPartAndroidBase" Abstract="True">
    <techLevel>Archotech</techLevel>
    <thingCategories Inherit="False">
      <li>AAH_BodyPartsAndroidArchotech</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Items/AAH_AndroidPart_Archotech</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>0.80</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <recipeMaker Inherit="False" />
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
